line	<str>At Betty's request, I met her at her uncle's home north west of the Tithe Farm, south of Hosidius. However, upon arrival, we found the Dead Body of her uncle. I examined the Body, searched the nearby area for Clues, and questioned potential Witnesses.</str>
line	<col=000080>I completed my investigation and uncovered a few things of note. I shared what I'd found with <col=800000>Betty</col>, but rather than going to <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col>, she suggested we head to <col=800000>Port Piscarilius</col>, where an old friend of her father lives. I should let her know when I'm ready to depart.</col>
step	10	24	Thrown in prison
line	<str>I completed my investigation and uncovered a few things of note. I shared what I'd found with Betty, but rather than going to Sergeant Hudson, she suggested we head to Port Piscarilius, where an old friend of her father lives. However, Sergeant Hudson was already there when arrived. He had us arrested and imprisoned in the Port Piscarilius Guardhouse for being present at a crime scene without reporting the crime.</str>
line	<col=000080>I spoke to <col=800000>Betty</col> and she made it clear that I needed to find out why <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> had already been in <col=800000>Port Piscarilius</col> when we arrived. To do so, I'll first need to find a away to escape the <col=800000>Port Piscarilius Guardhouse</col>.</col>
step	11	25	Escaping from prison
line	<col=000080>I spoke to <col=800000>Betty</col> and she made it clear that I needed to find out why <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> had already been in <col=800000>Port Piscarilius</col> when we arrived. To do so, I'll need to head over to the house of <col=800000>Captain Jensen</col>, the friend of <col=800000>Betty's</col> father. She lives in the north west corner of the city.</col>
step	12	26	Finding Captain Jensen's body
line	<col=000080>I spoke to <col=800000>Betty</col> and she made it clear that I needed to find out why <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> had already been in <col=800000>Port Piscarilius</col> when we arrived. To do so, I headed over to the house of <col=800000>Captain Jensen</col>, the friend of <col=800000>Betty's</col> father, in the north west corner of the city. However, upon arrival I found her <col=800000>Dead Body</col>. I need to try and work out what happened. Due to me now being wanted myself, I won't be able to question anyone, but I can still examine the <col=800000>Body</col> and search the house for <col=800000>Clues</col>.</col>
step	13	27	After finding enough evidence about Captain Jensen
line	<str>I spoke to Betty and she made it clear that I needed to find out why Sergeant Hudson had already been in Port Piscarilius when we arrived. To do so, I headed over to the house of Captain Jensen, the friend of Betty's father, in the north west corner of the city. However, upon arrival I found her Dead Body.</str>
line	{{Colour|#000080|Due to me now being wanted myself, I wasn't be able to question anyone, but I was still able to examine the <col=800000>Body</col> of <col=800000>Captain Jensen</col> and search the house for <col=800000>Clues</col>. When I'm ready, I should head back to the <col=800000>Port Piscarilius Guardhouse</col> and share what I've found with <col=800000>Betty</col>.}}
step	14	36	Arriving at Shayzien
line	<str>Due to me now being wanted myself, I wasn't be able to question anyone, but I was still able to examine the Body of Captain Jensen and search the house for Clues. With my investigation complete, I returned to the Port Piscarilius Guardhouse, but found that Betty was gone. In her place, an ominous message had been left.</str>
line	<col=000080>With no other option, I managed to use the <col=800000>Clues</col> I'd uncovered to determine that a Shayzien Leader was the next target. However, upon arriving at the <col=800000>Shayzien Encampment</col>, I found <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> there. I quickly found out that the <col=800000>Killer</col> had already struck. Despite his suspicions, <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> agreed to let me investigate this new murder, which took place west of the <col=800000>Shayzien Encampment</col>. I should do so by examining the <col=800000>Body</col>, searching the nearby area for <col=800000>Clues</col>, and questioning potential <col=800000>Witnesses</col>.</col>
step	15	37	After finding enough evidence about the Shayzien commissioner
line	<col=000080>With no other option, I managed to use the <col=800000>Clues</col> I'd uncovered to determine that a Shayzien Leader was the next target. However, upon arriving at the <col=800000>Shayzien Encampment</col>, I found <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> there. I quickly found out that the <col=800000>Killer</col> had already struck. Despite his suspicions, <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> agreed to let me investigate this new murder, which took place west of the <col=800000>Shayzien Encampment</col>. I examined the <col=800000>Body</col>, searched the nearby area for <col=800000>Clues</col>, and questioned potential <col=800000>Witnesses</col>. I should now let <col=800000>Sergeant Hudson</col> know what I've learnt.</col>
step	16	38	After sharing the evidence with Captain Hudson
line	<str>With no other option, I managed to use the Clues I'd uncovered to determine that a Shayzien Leader was the next target. However, upon arriving at the Shayzien Encampment, I found Sergeant Hudson there. I quickly found out that the Killer had already struck. Despite his suspicions, Sergeant Hudson agreed to let me investigate this new murder, which took place west of the Shayzien Encampment. I examined the Body, searched the nearby area for Clues, and questioned potential Witnesses.</str>
line	<col=000080>I completed my investigation and uncovered a few things of note. I shared what I'd found with Sergeant Hudson. He made it clear that to prove my innocence, I'll need to use the <col=800000>Clues</col> I've discovered to work out the location of the <col=800000>Killer</col>. To do so, I might need to revisit the previous crime scenes in <col=800000>Land's End</col>, south of <col=800000>Hosidius</col>, in the north west corner of <col=800000>Port Piscarilius</col> and west of the <col=800000>Shayzien Encampment</col>. Once I think I know the location of the <col=800000>Killer</col>, I should head there right away.</col>
step	17	40	Entering the hidden lair
line	<str>I completed my investigation and uncovered a few things of note. I shared what I'd found with Sergeant Hudson. He made it clear that to prove my innocence, I'll need to use the Clues I've discovered to work out the location of the Killer.</str>
line	<col=000080>Using the <col=800000>Clues</col> I'd discovered, I was able to determine that an island in the middle of the <col=800000>River Hos</col> was the location of the <col=800000>Killer</col>. I went to this island and found a <col=800000>Hidden Lair</col>. I should explore it and see what I can discover.</col>
done	<str>Using the Clues I'd discovered, I was able to determine that an island in the middle of the River Hos was the location of the Killer. However, upon my arrival there, I was attacked by Betty, who revealed that she was the one responsible for the murders. She claimed that her father killed her mother and sister and then, with the help of her other victims, covered it up. However, Sergeant Hudson then arrived, having followed the Clues himself. He revealed that Betty's mother and sister died of an illness, but that Betty had never been able to accept that. With no way out, Betty ultimately chose to kill herself rather than face justice.</str>
